  "provider": "edudzi-jira",
  "description": "Governed Jira Cloud automation for RailCall — ten commands covering the full issue lifecycle over the Jira REST API v3 (Basic Auth with an Atlassian API token stored in the RailCall vault; egress is allowlisted to *.atlassian.net and *.jira.com only).\n\nWHO IT'S FOR\nEngineering teams and solo developers who want an AI agent to run day-to-day Jira hygiene — triage, follow-up comments, status moves, assignment, evidence attachments — without handing out raw API credentials or letting writes happen unreviewed. Every mutating command is dry-run-first: RailCall previews the exact payload and requires explicit approval before anything touches your tracker, and each approved run produces a signed receipt.\n\nCOMMANDS (10)\nRead (low risk):\n- jira.getIssue — fetch one issue by key or numeric id (summary, status, assignee, full fields).\n- jira.searchIssues — JQL search via POST /rest/api/3/search/jql (the legacy GET /search was removed by Atlassian in 2025); token-based pagination (next_page_token / is_last), no total count.\n- jira.listIssueTypes — list issue types available in the instance, so agents pick valid types before creating.\nWrite (medium risk, approval-gated):\n- jira.createIssue — create an issue in a project; plain-text descriptions are auto-converted to Atlassian Document Format.\n- jira.updateIssue — edit summary and/or description of an existing issue.\n- jira.addComment — append a comment (also converted to ADF).\n- jira.transitionIssue — move an issue to a new status by transition id.\n- jira.assignUser — assign by Atlassian accountId or by email (resolved via /user/search).\n- jira.attachFile — upload an attachment (text or base64) with the required X-Atlassian-Token: no-check header.\nDestructive (high risk, approval-gated):\n- jira.deleteIssue — delete an issue, optionally including subtasks.\n\nQUICK START\n1. Create an API token: id.atlassian.com → Security → API tokens.\n2. In Studio → Integrations, add credential entry \"edudzi-jira\" (or \"jira\") with JIRA_DOMAIN, JIRA_EMAIL, JIRA_API_TOKEN. Credentials are read from the vault only — never from process environment variables.\n3. Install and open Studio: railcall market install edudzi-jira && railcall studio.\n4. Run jira.listIssueTypes to see valid types for your project, then jira.createIssue with {project_key: \"PROJ\", summary: \"Fix login bug\", issue_type: \"Bug\"} — approve the previewed payload and you get back {id, key, self}.\n\nERROR BEHAVIOR\nHTTP failures raise loudly and are never returned as data: field-level errors such as issuetype: \"Specify a valid issue type\" are surfaced verbatim so the agent can self-correct. Writes are never auto-retried, so a flaky network cannot create duplicate issues or comments. Note that issue types are project-specific — Jira Product Discovery projects accept only \"Idea\".\n\ncontest:2026Q3",
